@page "/"

<PageTitle>Home</PageTitle>

<section class="intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">.NET 11 · static server render</p>
    <h1>State that survives the next request</h1>
    <p class="lede">Each click is a new HTTP request. The component is gone when the response is sent. These two pages keep a flash message and a wizard draft anyway.</p>
</section>

<div class="cards">
    <a class="card" href="feedback">
        <p class="eyebrow">TempData</p>
        <h2>Feedback</h2>
        <p>Post a comment, redirect, and show the result once. Refresh clears the banner.</p>
    </a>
    <a class="card" href="onboarding">
        <p class="eyebrow">Session</p>
        <h2>Onboarding</h2>
        <p>A three-step draft that stays across requests, a new tab, and a refresh.</p>
    </a>
</div>
